# Expose the Culprit, "choose one or both" (CR 700.2): choosing no mode is refused; both modes on Bot1's own face-down Riftburst Hellion (cast face down with a Black
# Lotus). The modes happen in order: mode 1 turns it face up (it is a face-up creature with disguise at once), so mode 2, "exile any
# number of face-up creatures you control with disguise in a face-down pile, shuffle that pile, then cloak them", can take it: it is
# exiled and put back onto the battlefield face down as a cloaked 2/2 with ward {2} (CR 701.58a). A face-down creature never ends up
# face up, and the Hellion is a new object, untapped.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Riftburst Hellion
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Expose the Culprit
Plains x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Riftburst Hellion.Cast(Ability: Disguise)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield..FaceDown = true
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Expose the Culprit.Cast
! Bot1.Modes(Count: 0)
Bot1.Modes(1; 2)
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.#1)
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Riftburst Hellion)

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield..FaceDown = true
Bot1.Battlefield..FaceDownName = Riftburst Hellion
Bot1.Battlefield..Power = 2
Bot1.Battlefield..Tapped = false
Bot1.Graveyard = Expose the Culprit; Black Lotus
